@startuml
title Step 5 - Resource Instance State Machine
hide empty description
state "Planned\n(PLANNED)" as PLANNED
state "Provisioning\n(PROVISIONING)" as PROVISIONING
state "Ready\n(READY)" as READY
state "Failed\n(FAILED)" as FAILED
state "Retired\n(RETIRED)" as RETIRED

[*] --> PLANNED : planner chooses CREATE
PLANNED --> PROVISIONING : reconcile create/update
PROVISIONING --> READY : provider success / persist references
PROVISIONING --> FAILED : provider failure / persist actual state
READY --> PLANNED : planner chooses UPDATE / retain identity
READY --> READY : scope-safe REUSE / refresh state
READY --> READY : collectResourceOutputs / transient outputs
READY --> RETIRED : retire instance and active bindings / exclude from reuse
FAILED --> PLANNED : explicit retry/update
RETIRED --> [*]

note right of READY
  Canonical reuse starts from exact active ResourceInstanceBinding tuple.
  Owner columns are original ownership only, never an alternate read path.
  Cross-boundary reuse requires EXPLICIT_SHARED + matching key/policy.
end note
@enduml
